+// KFU (kfu_rulecheck_1110, Rule Checker; supersedes ECI bit 1; b1760): the turn's lists keep a foe or camp our own hit just killed. Bit 1:
+// after each successful attack or cast, visible foes within 6 that the engine reports dead go on this turn's dead list (the C&I partner
+// dies with them and reads dead too); aoe_best_tile, free_cast and every foe_model::unreachable test skip them. Bit 2: next_camp_in_reach (Varg's reset after
+// a splash) takes only camps alive in the engine. Bit 4 (bank_first t_hit, PHY row): a visible foe with two turns before my next turn
+// (the turn table) reaches the tribute one round sooner. 0 = v682.
+#define KFU_BITS 0
+inline const volatile int KFU_TAB[2] = { 0x4B465531, KFU_BITS };
+#define KFU_ON(b) ((KFU_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
+inline std::array<std::uint32_t, 12> kfu_dead_h{};
+inline int kfu_dead_n = 0, kfu_dead_r = -1000, kfu_dead_me = 0;
+// STL (stl_rulecheck_1110, Rule Checker; b1760; one bug-bar line with KFU): mid-turn staleness after my own actions. Bit 1: after my self-shield
+// cast, my shield is re-read (hold_capture, fight_volley_veto). Bit 2: a successful hit on a camp marks its group awake in W.camps and W.awake.
+// Bit 4: a champion target that died is followed by a re-read of my gems and gold (the win bank this turn). 0 = v682.
+#define STL_BITS 0
+inline const volatile int STL_TAB[2] = { 0x53544C31, STL_BITS };
+#define STL_ON(b) ((STL_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
